cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Glucocorticoid signalling tracks circadian output across human metabolic tissues"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying manuscript."
type: software
version: 2.13.6
date-released: 2026-11-17
abstract: >-
  Code for the manuscript of the same title. It builds every table and figure from public data:
  the association between glucocorticoid receptor expression and circadian clock output in
  thirteen estimates from seven human cohorts (adipose tissue, skeletal muscle and pancreatic
  islets), its specificity against all measured genes and all nuclear receptors, the prediction of
  one tissue from another, the within-person response to a hyperinsulinaemic clamp against a
  time-matched saline control, and the response to hydrocortisone. It infers circadian phase and
  amplitude from one sample per person and validates the inference against time series, and it
  compares four mechanisms for the forcing of a population of oscillators against the same
  observables, with a calibrated joint criterion and a confusion matrix that says which mechanisms
  the data can tell apart. Every run records its settings, the hash of every input and output, and
  whether it is a complete reproduction.
keywords:
  - circadian
  - glucocorticoid receptor
  - entrainment
  - phase coherence between tissues
  - insulin resistance
  - skeletal muscle
  - adipose tissue
  - transcriptomics
